    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for OpenEXR.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 8.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "OpenEXR is a high dynamic-range (HDR) image file format developed by Industrial Light & Magic for use in computer imaging applications. This package contains libraries and sample applications for handling the format. \n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* OpenEXR: OpenEXR: Out-of-bounds write vulnerability via crafted EXR files (CVE-2026-59184)\n\n* OpenEXR: OpenEXR: Heap out-of-bounds write via crafted tiled EXR file (CVE-2026-59186)\n\n* OpenEXR: OpenEXR: Information disclosure and denial of service due to out-of-bounds read (CVE-2026-59189)\n\n* OpenEXR: OpenEXR: Heap out-of-bounds write in exrmultiview via crafted EXR files (CVE-2026-68515)\n\n* OpenEXR: OpenEXR: Information disclosure and denial of service via out-of-bounds read (CVE-2026-59981)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
      {
